  "question": {
    "text": "An <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1800</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math> toaster, a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kW</mi></math> electric fan and a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math> lamp are plugged in the same <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> circuit i.e., all the three devices are in parallel. What is the approximate value of the total current (i.e. the sum of current drawn by the three devices) through the circuit?",
